@node STM8 Options
@section Options

@c man begin OPTIONS
@table @gcctabopt
@item --model=medium
@itemx --model=large
Select the code memory model.  The default is @code{medium}, with
16-bit code addresses; @code{large} uses 24-bit code addresses.
The @code{.stm8_model} directive also selects this model.  Conflicting
model selections in one object are rejected.

@item --relax
@itemx --no-relax
Enable or disable assembler relaxation of relative jumps to symbolic
addresses.  Relaxation is enabled by default.  A jump that cannot reach
its destination uses @code{JP} in the medium model or @code{JPF} in the
large model.  Conditional jumps invert their condition to skip the
absolute jump.  Jumps to undefined, weak or other-section symbols use
absolute relocations because their relative distance is unknown until
link time.  @code{CALLR} and @code{JRF} retain their original encoding.
@end table
@c man end

@node STM8 Syntax
@section Syntax and directives

Register names are case insensitive.  @samp{;} starts a comment and
@samp{#} starts a comment when it is the first character on a line.
Immediate operands have a @samp{#} prefix.  A memory operand with a
@samp{.s} suffix selects the short address encoding.

The @code{lo8}, @code{hi8} and @code{hh8} expression modifiers extract
successive bytes of an address, with relocations when needed.
The @code{.3byte} directive emits a big-endian 24-bit value.
The @code{.stm8_model "medium"} and @code{.stm8_model "large"} directives
select the code memory model and record it in the ELF object.
